# Preventive, not corrective: the repo is already LF in the index and the
# working tree. This pins that invariant so it does not depend on each
# developer's core.autocrlf.
#
# The deployment target is Linux (Raspberry Pi). A CRLF Makefile or shell
# script that reached the Pi would fail in ways that read as unrelated bugs,
# so eol=lf is set for the working tree too: what is edited here is
# byte-for-byte what the robot builds. No .bat/.cmd/.ps1 exist in this repo,
# so nothing needs CRLF.
#
# Note that `text=auto` will NOT retrofit a file already committed with CRLF;
# that would need a forced one-time pass. Nothing here needs one today.
* text=auto eol=lf

# text=auto already leaves detected binaries alone; these are explicit so a
# misfiring heuristic cannot corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
